From: mikkojhuttunen <mikkojhuttunen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:57:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cavity workbench: spatial hole burning panel

New panel under the spectrum shows spatial hole burning in the gain
crystal. With the best mode q lasing alone and its gain clamped at
threshold, the saturated gain along the crystal is g0/(1+S*I) with the
standing-wave intensity I = sin^2(kp) (linear cavity, or ring without
an isolator) or uniform intensity (ring with isolator, twisted-mode
pair); S follows from the clamping condition.

The upper plot zooms into three lambda/2n periods at a chosen depth in
the crystal and shows the lasing mode, the gain left at its nodes and a
neighbouring mode q+m whose pattern is shifted by 2*pi*m*p/p_rt. The
lower plot gives, for m = -40..40, the neighbour's net gain over loss
(hole-burning gain times its own gain-line and filter factor); bars
above 1 can start lasing. Bars are clickable. The note states the
result in words and flags when the results panel's simpler mode-count
rule disagrees. The model assumptions list the approximations.

Both editions regenerated.

